</td>
        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The FydeOS project has announced the release of <a href="fydeos">FydeOS</a> 23.0, a significant update of the project's ChromeOS-based Linux distribution that aims to bring a Google Chromebook-like experience to standard PCs. This new version upgrades the Android subsystem to Android 13: "<span class="Quote">We are delighted to announce the release of FydeOS 23 'Chromatic Cadence'. This release upgrades the underlying Chromium OS platform from r144 to r150 and introduces a new Android subsystem framework, refreshed system apps, and enhanced remote desktop capabilities for enterprise devices. FydeOS 23 focuses on strengthening the foundations of the operating system. These changes provide a more robust base for future improvements to app compatibility, system maintenance, and enterprise device management. FydeOS 23 upgrades the Android subsystem across all editions to Android 13 and introduces fyDroid, a new implementation for supporting Android apps on FydeOS. We plan to make fyDroid fully open source. Going forward, we will continue to develop this framework, progressively update its Android version, and improve app compatibility, performance and security.</span>" See the <a href="https://fydeos.io/blog/release-note-v23/">release announcement</a> for a full list of changes and screenshots. FydeOS is provided as separate BIN images for Intel or AMD processors; here are the <a href="https://fydeos.io/download/">download</a> links (<a href="table.php?distribution=fydeos&pkglist=true&version=23.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://download.fydeos.io/v23.0/FydeOS_for_PC_iris_v23.0-io.bin.zip">FydeOS_for_PC_iris_v23.0-io.bin.zip</a> (2,350MB, <a href="https://fydeos.io/download/pc/intel-iris/">SHA256</a>), <a href="https://download.fydeos.io/v23.0/FydeOS_for_PC_apu_v23.0-io.bin.zip">FydeOS_for_PC_apu_v23.0-io.bin.zip</a> (2,291MB, <a href="https://fydeos.io/download/pc/apu/">SHA256</a>).</td>
